---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Paver Blocks"
  description="Learn how Paver Blocks collects, uses, stores and protects information when you visit our website, request a quotation or contact our team."
  canonical="https://paverblocks.com.pk/privacy-policy/"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Your Privacy Matters</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>How Paver Blocks handles personal information when you browse our website, contact us or discuss a paving and construction project.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="policy-wrap">
    <div class="policy-meta">
      <span><strong>Effective date:</strong> 12 November 2026</span>
      <span><strong>Last updated:</strong> 12 November 2026</span>
    </div>

    <aside class="policy-callout">
      This policy explains our current website and enquiry practices. Some services, such as online checkout, payment processing and analytics, may depend on features being enabled. We will update this policy when our actual services or data practices change.
    </aside>

    <article class="policy-content">
      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>“Paver Blocks”, “we”, “us” and “our” refer to the Paver Blocks business represented publicly by Mithal Shahan, Civil Contractor, based in Hyderabad, Sindh, Pakistan.</p>
      <p><strong>Website:</strong> <a href="https://paverblocks.com.pk/">paverblocks.com.pk</a><br />
      <strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:hellopaverblocks@gmail.com">hellopaverblocks@gmail.com</a><br />
      <strong>Phone and WhatsApp:</strong> <a href="tel:+923162753210">+92 316 2753210</a><br />
      <strong>Location:</strong> Hyderabad, Sindh, Pakistan</p>
      <p>If a different registered legal entity is responsible for a particular transaction, its legal name and contact details should be provided in the relevant quotation, invoice or order documentation.</p>

      <h2>2. Scope of this policy</h2>
      <p>This policy applies to information collected through this website, our quotation and project enquiry forms, and communications you choose to have with us by telephone, email or WhatsApp. It also explains relevant third-party services used to operate and protect the website.</p>
      <p>It does not replace any separate terms, notices or contractual documents supplied for a specific project, product sale, payment or service.</p>

      <h2>3. Information we may collect</h2>
      <p>Depending on how you interact with us, we may collect the following categories of information:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Contact details:</strong> your name, telephone number, email address and preferred contact method.</li>
        <li><strong>Project and site details:</strong> project location, type of work, approximate area, budget information if provided, specifications, site conditions, requested timelines and the details you include in your message.</li>
        <li><strong>Order and transaction details:</strong> products or services requested, quantities, delivery information, order communications, payment status and records needed to manage a transaction. Where an external payment provider is used, payment-card details are handled by that provider rather than requested in our project enquiry form.</li>
        <li><strong>Communications and attachments:</strong> messages, photographs, drawings, documents or other information you voluntarily send to us by email, WhatsApp or another agreed channel.</li>
        <li><strong>Technical information:</strong> information that may be generated when you visit the website, such as IP address, browser and device details, approximate location inferred from network information, requested pages, timestamps, referring pages and security or diagnostic events.</li>
        <li><strong>Spam-protection information:</strong> technical signals and challenge responses used by Cloudflare Turnstile to help distinguish legitimate visitors from automated or abusive traffic.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Please do not send passwords, payment-card security codes, identity documents or sensitive personal information through the general project enquiry form unless we specifically request information through an appropriate secure process.</p>

      <h2>4. How information is collected</h2>
      <p>We collect information when you enter it into a website form, contact us by phone, email or WhatsApp, request a quotation, discuss or place an order, provide project documents, or otherwise communicate with our team.</p>
      <p>Some technical information may be collected automatically by the website infrastructure, hosting, security and diagnostic services used to deliver and protect the website.</p>

      <h2>5. How we use information</h2>
      <p>We may use information for purposes that include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Responding to enquiries and requests for quotations.</li>
        <li>Understanding project requirements, location, scope and feasibility.</li>
        <li>Preparing quotations, proposals, estimates and order documentation.</li>
        <li>Communicating about products, services, delivery, installation and project progress.</li>
        <li>Processing and administering orders and payments where those services are offered.</li>
        <li>Maintaining business, accounting, tax and transaction records.</li>
        <li>Protecting the website, preventing spam, fraud, misuse and unauthorized access.</li>
        <li>Diagnosing technical problems and improving website performance and usability.</li>
        <li>Meeting applicable legal obligations and establishing, exercising or defending legal claims.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not use the information in your project enquiry to send unrelated promotional messages unless you have asked to receive them or we otherwise have a lawful basis to do so. You can ask us to stop marketing communications at any time.</p>

      <h2>6. Our reasons for processing information</h2>
      <p>Depending on the circumstances and the laws that apply, we process information because it is necessary to respond to your request or take steps before entering a contract, perform an agreement, meet a legal obligation, protect our legitimate business and security interests, or because you have given consent where consent is required.</p>
      <p>Where we rely on consent, you may withdraw it. Withdrawal does not affect processing that took place before the withdrawal or processing that has another lawful basis.</p>

      <h2>7. When information may be shared</h2>
      <p>We do not sell personal information to data brokers. We may share limited information where reasonably necessary with:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Website and infrastructure providers:</strong> providers such as Cloudflare that support website hosting, delivery, security and bot protection.</li>
        <li><strong>Communication providers:</strong> email, telephone and messaging services used to communicate with you, including WhatsApp when you choose to contact us through it.</li>
        <li><strong>Payment providers:</strong> payment processors or financial institutions involved in a transaction, if an online or other electronic payment option is offered.</li>
        <li><strong>Project-related providers:</strong> suppliers, manufacturers, transporters, installers or contractors where sharing relevant project details is needed to prepare or fulfil your requested quotation or order.</li>
        <li><strong>Professional advisers and authorities:</strong> legal, accounting or other professional advisers, courts, regulators or law-enforcement authorities where disclosure is required or legally permitted.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We aim to share only information reasonably needed for the relevant purpose. Third-party services may process information under their own privacy terms and policies.</p>

      <h2>8. Cloudflare Turnstile and website security</h2>
      <p>Our quotation form uses Cloudflare Turnstile for spam and automated-submission protection when the secure form is enabled. Turnstile may process technical information and signals about your browser, device and interaction with the challenge to assess whether a submission is likely to be automated.</p>
      <p>Turnstile is a security service and is not intended to read the project details you enter into the form. Its processing is also subject to Cloudflare's own terms and privacy information. For more information, visit <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare's Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/turnstile/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Turnstile documentation</a>.</p>

      <h2>9. Cookies, local storage and analytics</h2>
      <p>Our website and its service providers may use cookies or similar technologies where needed for essential website functions, security, preferences or measurement. The exact technologies in use can change as website features are added or configured.</p>
      <p>The website's analytics configuration has not yet been fully verified for this policy publication. We will identify any analytics or advertising technologies actually enabled and update this notice accordingly. Where applicable law requires consent before non-essential cookies or similar technologies are used, those technologies should remain disabled until the required choice has been obtained.</p>
      <p>You can also manage cookies through your browser settings. Blocking certain technologies may affect website functionality or security checks.</p>

      <h2>10. International processing</h2>
      <p>Although our business is based in Pakistan, some website, communication, security or payment providers may operate infrastructure or process information in other countries. Where information is transferred internationally, we will take steps required by applicable law to provide appropriate protection, such as using contractual or other recognized safeguards where required.</p>
      <p>Privacy rights and regulatory requirements can differ depending on where you live. This policy is intended to explain our practices to visitors in Pakistan and elsewhere; it does not mean that every country's privacy law applies to every interaction.</p>

      <h2>11. How long we keep information</h2>
      <p>We keep personal information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purpose for which it was collected, including responding to enquiries, managing projects and orders, maintaining business records, resolving disputes, protecting the website and meeting legal obligations.</p>
      <p>Retention periods depend on the type of information and the circumstances. We have not stated a single fixed deletion period because enquiry, project, financial and security records can have different operational and legal requirements. When information is no longer needed, we will take reasonable steps to delete it, anonymize it or securely dispose of it, subject to applicable law and legitimate record-keeping needs.</p>

      <h2>12. How we protect information</h2>
      <p>We use reasonable technical and organizational measures intended to protect information against accidental loss, misuse, unauthorized access, alteration or disclosure. Website security measures may include encrypted connections, spam protection, restricted administrative access and service-provider security controls.</p>
      <p>No website, transmission method or storage system can be guaranteed to be completely secure. Please contact us promptly if you believe information you shared with us has been exposed or misused.</p>

      <h2>13. Your privacy choices and requests</h2>
      <p>Subject to applicable law and verification of your identity, you may contact us to request access to, correction of or deletion of personal information you have provided. You may also ask questions about how we use your information, object to certain processing, withdraw consent where processing is based on consent, or request that we stop sending promotional communications.</p>
      <p>Some information may need to be retained where required by law, for legitimate business record-keeping, to complete a transaction or to establish, exercise or defend legal claims. We will explain if we cannot fulfil a request in full.</p>
      <p>To make a request, email <a href="mailto:hellopaverblocks@gmail.com?subject=Privacy%20Request">hellopaverblocks@gmail.com</a> with the subject “Privacy Request”. Please describe the request and provide enough information for us to locate the relevant interaction. Do not email passwords or payment-card details. We may ask for reasonable information to verify that the request comes from the relevant person.</p>

      <h2>14. Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>This website and our services are intended for people seeking information about paving, construction, products or business services. They are not designed to target children. Please do not knowingly submit a child's personal information through the website. If you believe a child has provided personal information to us, contact us so we can review the matter and take appropriate steps.</p>

      <h2>15. Links to other websites and services</h2>
      <p>Our website may link to third-party websites or services, including WhatsApp and external provider websites. When you follow those links, the third party's own terms and privacy practices apply. We do not control third-party websites and encourage you to review their privacy information before sharing personal information with them.</p>

      <h2>16. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy when our website, services, technology, business practices or legal requirements change. The “Last updated” date at the top of this page indicates when the current version was published. Material changes will be reflected on this page.</p>

      <h2>17. Contact us</h2>
      <p>For privacy questions, concerns or requests, contact:</p>
      <p><strong>Paver Blocks — Privacy Enquiries</strong><br />
      By Mithal Shahan, Civil Contractor<br />
      Hyderabad, Sindh, Pakistan<br />
      Email: <a href="mailto:hellopaverblocks@gmail.com">hellopaverblocks@gmail.com</a><br />
      Phone / WhatsApp: <a href="tel:+923162753210">+92 316 2753210</a></p>
      <p>If you are located in a country with a privacy regulator and believe your applicable rights have not been respected, you may also have the right to raise a concern with the relevant supervisory authority in your country.</p>
    </article>

    <div class="policy-bottom">
      <p>Questions about how your information is handled?</p>
      <a class="button button-primary" href="mailto:hellopaverblocks@gmail.com?subject=Privacy%20Question">Contact us about privacy</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>

